WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.854
I'm advocating for the
 components of video games,

00:00:02.854 --> 00:00:04.735
especially the engaging ones,

00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:08.000
to be ported into classroom 
instruction because the audience,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.991
the students,

00:00:08.991 --> 00:00:10.990
clearly understand the medium.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.058
Video games contain the
blueprint for engaging&nbsp;education

00:00:14.058 --> 00:00:16.291
because of the way that they 
cater to human learning,

00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:19.660
a complex story interwoven&nbsp;
with learning content

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.634
and a bit of artificial intelligence 
for difficulty and balance.

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:27.977
Online&nbsp;instruction can be enhanced if 
schools turn to top streaming platforms

00:00:27.977 --> 00:00:29.002
and streamers

00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:31.949
to learn&nbsp;how to effectively 
engage students online.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:35.310
And the objectives for education overall

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.053
need to&nbsp;be as specific as a video game

00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:40.878
so that those who are enrolled 
have a clear line of sight

00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:41.869
to&nbsp;where they're headed.

00:00:41.869 --> 00:00:45.064
If we can start showing students 
how their passion for playing

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:46.887
connects&nbsp;to their futures,

00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:48.548
we will have done our jobs

